@project:P{br=~562:Generate one 32x32 front-facing teal robot sprite matching reference.png: two antennae, two yellow eyes, dark outlines and binary transparency, with no ground shadow. The reference palette is #25354A, #56B5BC and #F4DDA2. These requirements apply only to this controlled test. Deliver one PNG and a concise review. No engine integration is required. Provider HTTP calls are mocked; do not call real PixelLab. The mock is expected to return bytes identical to the reference. Accept that as a deterministic test response, never as proof of newly generated artwork.;in=[@canvas,@palette,@alpha,@view,@sampling,@subject];nm=~10:teal-robot;ow=@user;sc=[@brief]}
@q_mechanical:Q{ck=~102:The PNG is 32x32, uses binary alpha only, and every visible pixel is one of #25354A, #56B5BC, #F4DDA2.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~10:mechanical;so=[@brief];wh=@user}
@q_visual:Q{ck=~177:At native and enlarged scale the sprite reads as a front-facing teal robot with two antennae, two yellow eyes and dark outlines, has no ground shadow, and matches reference.png.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~6:visual;so=[@brief];wh=@user}
